# Cloudflare Pages redirects/rewrites for the TirraMind public site.
#
# Pages uses this Netlify-compatible file, NOT vercel.json or netlify.toml.
# Those two are left in the repo unused, so either vendor stays available.
#
# Syntax:  <from>  <to>  <status>
#   200 with an absolute destination = proxy (rewrite, URL stays put)
#   301/302                          = visible redirect
# Order matters: first match wins, so the catch-all must come last.
#
# LIMIT: Cloudflare Pages caps this file at 2000 rules (100 dynamic). We use
# well under that, but keep it in mind before adding per-path entries.

# Checkout is the Paddle.js overlay on /pricing — Paddle Billing has no static
# reusable checkout links. Keep old /buy links working.
/buy                /pricing                                        302

# ── Backend proxy ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Status 200 = the browser stays on tirramind.com while Pages fetches from the
# API host. This keeps the API same-origin from the browser's perspective, so
# subscriber keys aren't sent cross-origin and CORS never enters the picture.
#
# REQUIRES api.tirramind.com to exist and serve TLS. Until the VM is deployed
# these four rules resolve to nothing — see docs/research/production_deployment.md.
/brief.json         https://api.tirramind.com/brief.json            200
/brief.md           https://api.tirramind.com/brief.md              200
/api/v1/*           https://api.tirramind.com/api/v1/:splat         200
/evidence/*         https://api.tirramind.com/evidence/:splat       200

# ── Clean URLs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# /pricing -> pricing.html. Must be last: it matches everything.
/*                  /:splat.html                                    200
